# Kindling repo maintenance rules

These rules apply **only inside the canonical kindling repo** (marked by `KINDLING_REPO` at the root). For consumer repos, see `kindling-consumer.mdc`.

Mirrors **`.claude/rules/kindling-repo-maintenance.md`**. Keep both files aligned when editing.

## What this repo is

Kindling is the **plugin-layer template** for Hearth — a skeleton consumer that also provides tooling and templates for Hearth plugin repos.

```
skeleton (.skeleton/)  — process tooling
    └── kindling      — Hearth plugin contract + templates
```

## Mandatory sync: cursor ↔ claude rules

`kindling-consumer.mdc` and `.claude/rules/kindling-consumer.md` **must stay identical in content**. When editing one, update the other in the same commit.

Same rule applies to this file and its Claude mirror.

## kindling.manifest discipline

`kindling.manifest` is the authoritative list of all kindling-origin files. It has two categories:

1. **Syncignored** — listed in `kindling.manifest` AND `.syncignore`. These stay inside `.kindling/` and are never copied to consumer roots.
2. **Materialized** — listed in `kindling.manifest` only. These ARE copied to consumer roots on `init-kindling` / `sync-kindling`.

When adding a new file that consumers should receive:
- Add `source|destination` to `kindling.manifest`
- Do **not** add it to `.syncignore`
- Document in `CHANGELOG.md`

When adding a kindling-internal file:
- Add `source|destination` to `kindling.manifest`
- Add `destination` to `.syncignore`
- Document in `CHANGELOG.md`

## Bundled skeleton scripts

`scripts/init-skeleton.sh` and `scripts/skeleton-ignore.sh` are verbatim copies from `.skeleton/scripts/`. Keep them in sync:

```bash
diff scripts/init-skeleton.sh .skeleton/scripts/init-skeleton.sh
diff scripts/skeleton-ignore.sh .skeleton/scripts/skeleton-ignore.sh
```

Both diffs must be empty before committing.

## Templates

`templates/plugin-python/` is a scaffold reference — it is **not** automatically applied to consumer repos. It uses `{{ token }}` placeholders that must be substituted at `kindling new <slug>` time (or manually).

Do not add templates to `kindling.manifest` unless you want every consumer repo to receive them on sync.

## Testing changes

Before pushing any script change, test manually:

```bash
mkdir /tmp/test-$(date +%s) && cd /tmp/test-*
git init && git remote add origin git@github.com:test/test-plugin.git
cp /path/to/kindling/init-kindling .
chmod +x init-kindling
./init-kindling
# Verify submodules, wrappers, and rule files are present
```

## CHANGELOG.md

Always add an entry under `[Unreleased]` when changing:
- Scripts in `scripts/`
- Files in `kindling.manifest` or `.syncignore`
- `kindling-consumer.mdc` / `.claude/rules/kindling-consumer.md`
- Anything else that consumer repos will receive on `sync-kindling`

## Branch policy

- `main` is the production branch; consumer repos track it.
- Never force-push `main`.
- Use `fix/…` or `feat/…` branches for changes; merge via PR.
